    "numberEncoding": "Every i64 field (priceCents, requiredBuyBackValueCents, requiredMarketValueCents) is a DECIMAL STRING, because signed 64-bit values exceed JavaScript's safe integer range and a bare numeric literal would be rounded by JSON.parse before any code saw it. Parse them into BigInt. u32 fields stay JSON numbers — they cannot overflow.",
