    "note": "This is the step that names the PRIZE rather than the position. A draw verified against 0x01 odds proves you legitimately won slot i; only 0x03 proves what was in slot i. The preimage embeds the raw edition_fingerprint bytes, so 0x03 closes over 0x01 — verify this and the odds beneath it are transitively verified.",
    "hashedBytesNotJson": "snapshot_hash is sha256 of the CANONICAL BYTES below, never of the body JSON. The body is a separate rendering of the same input, so whitespace, key order or a different JSON library can never move the content address. A verifier must parse the body into these fields and rebuild the preimage — hashing the received bytes directly would reject a legitimately re-serialised body.",
    "utf8Trap": "displayedMedia is the ONLY variable-width field in any of the three preimages: a u32 BE length prefix followed by UTF-8 BYTES. In a language whose strings are UTF-16 (JavaScript), string.length is code units, not bytes, and the two differ for any non-ASCII character. Every ASCII-only case passes either way, so the multi-byte-displayed-media vector below is what makes this family bite.",
    "numberEncoding": "displayedValueCents is a DECIMAL STRING for the same reason the 0x01 cents fields are (ADR-KAN-36 §7): it is signed 64-bit and a bare JSON numeric literal would be rounded by JSON.parse before any verifier saw it. Parse it into BigInt. slotIndex and slotCount stay JSON numbers — they are u32 and cannot overflow.",
    "layout": [
      "domain: 1 byte = 0x03",
      "editionFingerprint: 32 bytes, the hex-DECODED digest (not its 64 ASCII characters)",
      "slotCount: u32 BE",
      "per slot, ASCENDING slotIndex: slotIndex u32 BE, currentItemId 16 bytes raw UUID big-endian (most-significant long first), displayedValueCents i64 BE signed, displayedMedia u32 BE byte-length prefix + UTF-8 bytes"
    ],
